comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T14:47:47.731Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check (all statuses): searched tsx,4.23.9,dependency update,and toolchain lineage. pm-a2g6 is the closed historical compatible-bump tranche; pm-ksr40d and pm-do5b are distinct open major migrations with explicit compatibility blockers. No current item owns this patch refresh,so this dated child under pm-u9d0 is canonical."
  "2026-08-07T14:48:40.003Z","harness:codex","Relationship rationale: pm-a2g6 is the completed compatible-bump precedent; pm-ksr40d and pm-do5b are the two intentionally deferred incompatible major tracks. Keeping all three edges makes the patch-versus-major decision legible in the project graph."
  "2026-08-07T14:49:08.522Z","harness:codex","Registry correction: the initial live lookup observed 4.23.9, but the install transaction reported 4.23.11 and a fresh npm registry query confirmed 4.23.11 with Node >=18. The canonical item and acceptance criteria now target 4.23.11 before final verification."
  "2026-08-07T14:58:11.065Z","harness:codex","Final evidence: package.json and pnpm-lock.yaml resolve registry-current tsx 4.23.11 (Node >=18); pnpm's fresh-release exception is explicit in pnpm-workspace.yaml. pnpm outdated now reports only the two canonical incompatible majors pm-ksr40d and pm-do5b. pnpm audit reports 0 vulnerabilities across 357 dependencies, and the exact dependency head passes all 6,938 tests at 100/100/100/100 plus the full quality/security/package gate."
  "2026-08-07T14:59:35.218Z","harness:codex","Changelog evidence: latest registry pm-changelog 2026.8.7 installed and generated CHANGELOG.md from 1,959 closed items; the immediate --check rerun reported unchanged."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-07T14:58:11.609Z","harness:codex","Re-query the registry after an install reports a newer version than the initial inventory; dependency state can advance within one delivery run, and exact-head evidence must name the version actually locked."
